# purpose: CI on every push and pull request: the full warscape-core `wsc gates` set, and the proxy DLL build, host tests and wine smoke test (job proxy).
# `proxy`, `viewer` and `harness-windows` run only when the branch changes their inputs and that input tree has not passed already
# (job `changes`, J54 below); a skipped job counts as passed for
# required checks and auto-merge (D32), so a brief or plan branch does not wait for the slow Windows runner.
# J57: a failed `changes` job must not skip them (a skip counts as passed): each slow job's `if:` starts with `!cancelled()` (no implicit success()) and
# runs whenever `needs.changes.result != 'success'`; its pass-marker steps still see an empty tree output and save nothing.
# Generated blocks: the `changes` and `notify` jobs, the `if:` of each slow job and its pass-marker steps come from the core (`wsc ci render`, wsc.toml [ci]);
# edit this template, then run `python3 core/wsc.py ci render` and commit both files.
# usage: runs on GitHub Actions; locally: python3 core/wsc.py gates
# when: automatic; require the "gates" check in branch protection for main.
# not-a-verb: GitHub runs workflows by file; this one only calls `wsc gates`.
# The core submodule is public (D29); checkout still passes WARSCAPE_CORE_TOKEN (D20), so keep the secret unless this step changes.
# workflow_dispatch chases a flaky harness case (J19): only harness-windows runs, with -Only/-Repeat; e.g.
#   gh workflow run gates.yml --ref <branch> -f only='hang watchdog' -f repeat=10
# It has its own concurrency group, so it neither cancels nor is cancelled by the push run on the same ref.
# One run per commit (J42): this workflow runs on push only, never on pull_request. A push to a branch with an open pull request used
# to start two whole runs (push and pull_request have different github.refs, so the concurrency group did not dedupe them). Checks
# attach to the commit, so the pull request still shows `gates`, `proxy` and `harness-windows` from this push run on its head commit and
# `gh pr merge --auto` still sees them (D32, D33); a branch with no pull request yet still gets CI on its first push; `policy` needs the
# pull request (its base and head) and lives in policy.yml, which runs nothing else. Route proved on PR #57 (jobs/J42/report.md).
# A newer push cancels an older run on the same branch (that commit is no longer the head auto-merge waits for), never on main.
# notify: a failed run on a branch with an open pull request comments once on it (`wsc ci notify`), so a red check is told.
# Rule 79 for CI (J54): a slow job (proxy, viewer, harness-windows) that already passed on this exact input tree is skipped. On success
# each saves a pass marker as its last step: actions/cache key `ci-pass-<salt>-<set>-<tree hash>` (`wsc ci inputs` hashes the
# set's files at HEAD: mode, object, path; bump `salt` in wsc.toml [ci] to invalidate every marker), holding the run id, attempt and commit that passed.
# `changes` restores each changed set's key; a hit skips the job and writes one step-summary line naming the set, the hash and the run
# that passed it, so the D31 fallback (`gh run download <that run> -n proxy-d3d9-napoleon` / `-n viewer-wasm`) still finds the build.
# Fails safe: a cache error, an empty hash or a marker that cannot be read runs the job. A workflow_dispatch run neither reads nor writes
# markers. Caches are scoped by branch (GitHub: a run restores caches of its own branch or the default branch, never a sibling's; entries
# unused for 7 days are evicted): a main push can only find markers written on main, a branch also finds main's.
name: gates
on:
  push:
  workflow_dispatch:
    inputs:
      only:
        description: 'harness integration case-name regex (empty: all cases)'
        type: string
        default: ''
      repeat:
        description: 'run each selected case this many times in a row'
        type: string
        default: '1'
permissions:
  contents: read
concurrency:
  group: gates-${{ github.ref }}${{ github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch' && format('-dispatch-{0}', github.run_id) || '' }}
  cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.ref != 'refs/heads/main' }}
jobs:
{{wsc changes}}
  gates:
    if: github.event_name != 'workflow_dispatch'
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 10
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v5
        with:
          submodules: true
          token: ${{ secrets.WARSCAPE_CORE_TOKEN }}
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v6
        with:
          python-version: '3.12'
      # the depth-1 submodule fetch brings the core tip's tag but not the pinned one once the core has a newer tag, and core_pin then
      # fails with "untagged commit" (v0.3.0, PR #55 run 40962535611): fetch the pinned tag; a missing tag is left to core_pin to report
      - run: |
          pin=$(python -c "import tomllib; print(tomllib.load(open('wsc.toml', 'rb'))['core']['version'])")
          git -C core fetch --depth=1 --no-tags origin "refs/tags/$pin:refs/tags/$pin" || echo "could not fetch core tag $pin"
      # J79 (audit G13): the host-test packages, hash-locked (upscale/requirements-ci.txt says how the hashes were made), so the art, font and
      # x86re tests run here instead of skipping; a package whose wheel no longer matches its pinned sha256 fails this step, never the lock
      - run: python -m pip install --require-hashes -r upscale/requirements-ci.txt
      - run: python core/wsc.py gates
  # proxy: build the proxy d3d9.dll with the release route (mingw-w64 i686 on Ubuntu 24.04, the same toolchain as the PC's
  # `build.sh --docker`: proxy/README.md "Build", D31) and run its host tests; the DLL is kept as a workflow artifact.
  proxy:
    needs: changes
{{wsc if proxy}}
    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
    timeout-minutes: 30   # RmlUi compiles in this job (core ci/gates.yml.in has 30; J64 raised it from 15)
    steps:
      # a shallow checkout is enough: the build id hashes the DLL inputs' content at HEAD (core/proxy/tools/build_id.py, J45), not history
      - uses: actions/checkout@v5
        with:
          submodules: true   # the proxy sources, tools and the harness live in the core since J12
          token: ${{ secrets.WARSCAPE_CORE_TOKEN }}
      - name: the pinned mingw-w64 toolchain (core/proxy/tools/toolchain.py apt; core 0.27.0, W24)
        run: |
          sudo apt-get update -q
          sudo apt-get install -y -q --no-install-recommends $(python3 core/proxy/tools/toolchain.py apt)
          dpkg-query -W -f '${Package}=${Version}\n' '*mingw-w64*'
{{wsc fetch_cache}}
      - run: core/proxy/tools/build.sh all
      - name: the DLL is byte-identical when built from another checkout path
        run: core/proxy/tools/build.sh repro
      - name: smoke test the DLL under wine (a stand-in exe loads it; guard verdicts, config, log, clean detach)
        run: |
          sudo dpkg --add-architecture i386 && sudo apt-get update -q
          sudo DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive apt-get install -y -q --no-install-recommends wine wine32:i386
          core/proxy/tools/build.sh smoke
      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: proxy-d3d9-napoleon
          path: build/proxy/napoleon/d3d9.dll
          if-no-files-found: error
{{wsc pass_marker proxy}}

  # viewer: build the review viewer to wasm inside the emsdk image pinned in viewer/pins.json (the same container as the PC's
  # `build.sh --docker`, D30/D31), prove float32 Lua under Node, then render hello-world in headless Chromium and run its checks
  # (tests/test_viewer.py). viewer.js, viewer.wasm, their sha256 and the renders are kept as a workflow artifact (J31).
  viewer:
    needs: changes
{{wsc if viewer}}
    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
    timeout-minutes: 20
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v5
        with:
          submodules: true   # the viewer pin tests read core/proxy/tools (fetch_lua.py), in the core since J12
          token: ${{ secrets.WARSCAPE_CORE_TOKEN }}
      # the container runs as root: hand build/ back to the runner user for the render steps
      - run: viewer/core/build.sh --docker all && sudo chown -R "$(id -u):$(id -g)" build
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v6
        with:
          python-version: '3.12'
      - run: python -m pip install -q playwright==1.64.1 && python -m playwright install --with-deps chromium
      - run: python -m unittest tests.test_viewer tests.test_uikit -v
      # J34: the library's lint, the four-corner gate on the board and the changes report against uikit/napoleon/baseline.json
      - run: python uikit/napoleon/lint.py
      - run: python uikit/napoleon/gate.py --out build/viewer/out/uikit_gate
      - run: python uikit/napoleon/changes.py
      - name: renders kept with the build (1080p x 1.0, 4K x 125 % = dp ratio 2.5)
        run: |
          python viewer/core/render.py --size 1920x1080 --dp-ratio 1.0 --out build/viewer/out/hello_1080p_r1.png | tee -a build/viewer/out/renders.txt
          python viewer/core/render.py --size 3840x2160 --dp-ratio 2.5 --out build/viewer/out/hello_4k_slider125.png | tee -a build/viewer/out/renders.txt
          (cd build/viewer/out && sha256sum *.png >> SHA256SUMS && cat SHA256SUMS)
      # always: a red run keeps its diff PNGs (build/viewer/out/uikit_gate, J80), written by changes.py and by the baseline test in tests/test_uikit.py
      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        if: always()
        with:
          name: viewer-wasm
          path: build/viewer/out/
          if-no-files-found: error
{{wsc pass_marker viewer}}

  # harness-windows: the J2 watcher, lock, profiles, hang watchdog, updater and installer on GitHub's Windows runner under
  # Windows PowerShell 5.1 (shell: powershell), the same PowerShell the PC runs. Fake games are compiled on the runner.
  harness-windows:
    needs: changes
    # a workflow_dispatch run exists only to run this job (J19 -Only/-Repeat), whatever the branch changed
{{wsc if harness dispatch}}
    runs-on: windows-latest
    timeout-minutes: 25
    env:
      CI: 'true'
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v5
        with:
          submodules: true   # the proxy sources, tools and the harness live in the core since J12
          token: ${{ secrets.WARSCAPE_CORE_TOKEN }}
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v6
        with:
          python-version: '3.12'
      - name: PowerShell version
        shell: powershell
        run: $PSVersionTable.PSVersion.ToString()
      # J22: the Python host tests that run bash, on Windows: they must find Git Bash themselves (tools/verbs/setup.py git_bash), never
      # the WSL launcher, which the gates job on Linux cannot show. job.sh calls python3, which setup-python does not provide here.
      - name: Python host tests that run bash (Git Bash found explicitly)
        timeout-minutes: 3
        shell: powershell
        run: |
          $py = (Get-Command python).Source
          $py3 = Join-Path (Split-Path $py) 'python3.exe'
          if (-not (Test-Path $py3)) { Copy-Item $py $py3 }
          python -m unittest tests.test_job_sh tests.test_pc_deploy tests.test_claude_hook tests.test_setup tests.test_proxy_host.GitBash
          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }
      # J74 (audit G3, H9): the PowerShell installer, the play script and the pack installer run only on Windows; -v lists every test as ok or skipped
      # in the log, and the three modules fail (never skip) here when PowerShell is missing.
      - name: PowerShell installer, play and pack-installer tests
        timeout-minutes: 8
        shell: powershell
        run: |
          python -m unittest -v tests.test_release_installer tests.test_play tests.test_install_packs
          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }
      - name: harness host tests (unit and integration)
        # shorter than the job timeout: a hung test fails the step and the job still ends, so its log is kept
        timeout-minutes: 18
        shell: powershell
        # inputs arrive through env, never pasted into the script; on push they are empty: the full suite, once
        env:
          HT_ONLY: ${{ inputs.only }}
          HT_REPEAT: ${{ inputs.repeat || '1' }}
        run: ./core/harness/tests/Run-HostTests.ps1 -Suite $(if ($env:HT_ONLY) { 'integration' } else { 'all' }) -Only $env:HT_ONLY -Repeat ([int]$env:HT_REPEAT)
{{wsc pass_marker harness shell=bash}}

  # notify: the last job; a failure in any job above, on a branch with an open pull request, comments once there (D32: a failed check
  # leaves the pull request open; this makes it impossible to miss). The only job with write access, and only to pull requests.
{{wsc notify gates needs=changes,gates,proxy,viewer,harness-windows}}
